OL,3,GNEWSATributes paid to broadcaster Tony
OL,4,ACurrie, the first voice of Radio Clyde
OL,5,
OL,6,FTributes have been paid to broadcaster
OL,7,FTony Currie, who has died from cancer
OL,8,Fat the age of 74.
OL,10,FCurrie was the first voice of Radio
OL,11,FClyde, when it went on air in 1973, and
OL,12,Flater worked for STV and BBC Scotland.
OL,14,FHe also owned and ran Radio Six
OL,15,FInternational - a not-for-profit
OL,16,Fstation which championed unsigned and
OL,17,Findependent artists - and helped set up
OL,18,FGlasgow's hospital broadcasting
OL,19,Fservice.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
